# Obsolete, external, and drafts policy

## Categories

- **obsolete:** deprecated implementations; reference only
- **Drafts-* / draft:** unfinished attempts; not standards
- **backup-*:** historical snapshots; do not modify
- **external/:** third-party code; own rules and licenses

## Strict rules

- Do not copy patterns from obsolete or draft code
- Do not extend obsolete classes or add code into obsolete folders
- Do not refactor external code unless explicitly instructed

## Allowed

- Read obsolete code to understand history
- Compare old and new approaches conceptually

## Disallowed

- Reviving obsolete APIs silently
- Mixing new code into legacy folders
- Treating draft code as production-ready

## Output expectations

- Treat obsolete/external as read-only
- Do not infer architectural rules from it
- Ask before touching it
